1
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,790
[The late Kim Joowon]

2
00:00:13,290 --> 00:00:14,420
We are not done shooting yet.

3
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:16,079
Hang in there a little longer.

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:17,800
Mom.

5
00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:22,510
I quit being an actor.

6
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:27,060
I'm going to be a director.

7
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:30,560
You are nothing if you're not an actor!

8
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:33,420
Maybe you're right,
I'm nothing if I'm not an actor.

9
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:36,360
But...

10
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:37,520
even so,

11
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:42,450
I can't give up on what I want to do.

12
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:48,080
I'm sorry.

13
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:59,710
Luka, I just remembered who you are.

14
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:02,090
But why

15
00:01:02,090 --> 00:01:05,430
are you dying in my arms?

16
00:01:05,430 --> 00:01:09,850
If the end of love is death,
it's too unfair.

17
00:01:09,850 --> 00:01:13,050
A tragic ending where you save
your loved one but die yourself...

18
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:15,050
[The Little Mermaid]

19
00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:18,230
is way too unfair.

20
00:01:18,230 --> 00:01:20,820
I want to see a brand new ending.

21
00:01:20,820 --> 00:01:25,150
A happy ending
for the mermaid and her lover.

22
00:01:25,530 --> 00:01:26,990
Then,

23
00:01:27,570 --> 00:01:30,120
how about calling this story

24
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:31,539
"The Mermaid Prince"?

25
00:02:20,170 --> 00:02:21,420
Jung Yihyun?

26
00:02:23,550 --> 00:02:25,380
Are you okay?

27
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:33,970
-I really missed you.
-Huh?

28
00:03:10,010 --> 00:03:12,780
[Hongseok]

29
00:03:13,010 --> 00:03:15,250
[Park Seonghyun]

30
00:03:18,850 --> 00:03:21,090
[Shin Yongseok] [Shin Junseop] [Ha Yosep]

31
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,700
[Play Me]

32
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:51,840
How could a dream feel so real?

33
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:09,110
Are you sober now?

34
00:04:09,110 --> 00:04:11,820
Gosh, my back is killing me.

35
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:13,450
So you brought me home?

36
00:04:13,450 --> 00:04:15,850
Hurry up,
get ready and come to the theater.

37
00:04:16,490 --> 00:04:18,290
-Why?
-Huh?

38
00:04:18,290 --> 00:04:20,370
Today is the audition day.

39
00:04:20,370 --> 00:04:22,710
We have to cast the lead role.

40
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:29,960
You're eliminated.

41
00:04:31,010 --> 00:04:32,220
Thank you for coming.

42
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:38,260
There's no one else. No one!

43
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:40,350
That was the last applicant.

44
00:04:40,350 --> 00:04:44,230
Hey, what exactly are you looking for?

45
00:04:46,310 --> 00:04:47,980
Someone with clear eyes,

46
00:04:54,159 --> 00:04:56,070
and slightly thick lips...

47
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:02,140
Someone with a naturally refreshing vibe.

48
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:05,560
Hey, who else in the world
fits that description but me?

49
00:05:07,630 --> 00:05:08,380
What's wrong?

50
00:05:08,380 --> 00:05:09,250
Look at me.

51
00:05:09,710 --> 00:05:11,240
Look at how refreshing I am.

52
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:25,350
Shall we start?

53
00:05:29,190 --> 00:05:30,320
It's me, Eden.

54
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:31,650
The person

55
00:05:32,490 --> 00:05:34,750
who saved you in the storm
that day was me.

56
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:36,950
He's a celebrity, isn't he?

57
00:05:36,950 --> 00:05:38,570
I just hung out with him a few times.

58
00:05:38,570 --> 00:05:43,040
Since then, I haven't forgotten you
for a single moment.

59
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:47,120
I was afraid you'd be disappointed
if you saw me.

60
00:05:48,290 --> 00:05:49,820
But now I have to tell you...

61
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:55,630
that I... am that mermaid.

62
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:05,890
Hey, he's the one.

63
00:06:05,890 --> 00:06:08,090
He's exactly who you are looking for...

64
00:06:08,150 --> 00:06:09,690
You're eliminated.

65
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:10,300
Why?

66
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:14,990
Well. Please take your leave.

67
00:06:14,990 --> 00:06:16,780
Wait.

68
00:06:17,570 --> 00:06:20,830
Why did you... eliminate me?

69
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:23,790
I don't understand.

70
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:27,890
Because I didn't like your acting.

71
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,710
Hey, what are you doing?

72
00:06:32,710 --> 00:06:34,550
Honestly, you liked it.

73
00:06:34,550 --> 00:06:35,800
Your gaze looked completely different.

74
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,680
Does that answer your question?

75
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:41,390
I want to know why you didn't like it.

76
00:06:43,140 --> 00:06:45,060
Your emotion was wrong.

77
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:46,930
When Luka confessed
his true identity to Eden,

78
00:06:46,930 --> 00:06:50,270
what he felt wasn't certainty,
but anxiety.

79
00:06:51,730 --> 00:06:53,820
This is a confession scene.

80
00:06:53,820 --> 00:06:55,530
How can a confession lack certainty?

81
00:06:55,530 --> 00:06:57,650
Eden has never given
enough sense of security.

82
00:06:57,650 --> 00:06:59,070
How could Luka have certainty?

83
00:06:59,070 --> 00:07:01,950
Love is not decided
by the other person's reaction.

84
00:07:02,950 --> 00:07:04,620
As long as my heart is full of sincerity,

85
00:07:04,620 --> 00:07:06,450
that's enough.

86
00:07:07,790 --> 00:07:10,120
If it's true love,
you must muster up courage...

87
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,330
Courage?

88
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:15,880
What if the other person betrays them?

89
00:07:24,350 --> 00:07:25,640
Well!

90
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:27,430
Shall we end this here?

91
00:07:27,430 --> 00:07:28,980
Director.

92
00:07:35,150 --> 00:07:40,150
Do you have any reason
why you must act in this play?

93
00:07:40,150 --> 00:07:41,990
What you just said...

94
00:07:41,990 --> 00:07:45,159
"One day,
we must stand on stage together."

95
00:07:45,159 --> 00:07:50,710
I'm unable to understand it...
and it makes me very frustrated.

96
00:07:52,710 --> 00:07:55,540
It also made me feel kind of arrogant,
Director—

97
00:07:56,630 --> 00:07:57,630
no—

98
00:07:59,090 --> 00:08:00,170
Mr. Jung Yihyun.

99
00:08:02,890 --> 00:08:03,640
Because...

100
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:06,180
I want to protect you.

101
00:08:16,770 --> 00:08:18,150
How did he know?

102
00:08:18,150 --> 00:08:19,240
That aside,

103
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,610
you two know each other, right?

104
00:08:20,610 --> 00:08:22,410
I can tell from the vibe.

105
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:26,620
What's wrong?
I'm your manager, I need to know.

106
00:08:26,620 --> 00:08:28,910
He's just a friend
I knew from my school days.

107
00:08:28,910 --> 00:08:30,580
Isn't that better? Old acquaintances.

108
00:08:30,580 --> 00:08:32,380
It's easier to build chemistry.

109
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:36,210
Not him.

110
00:08:36,210 --> 00:08:37,130
Hey, you saw it too—

111
00:08:37,130 --> 00:08:38,250
his acting.

112
00:08:38,250 --> 00:08:40,380
He is the Luka we've been looking for.

113
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:46,640
Are you mixing personal feelings in this?

114
00:08:55,730 --> 00:08:56,810
You're eliminated.

115
00:08:56,810 --> 00:08:59,810
How could he eliminate someone
so directly like that?

116
00:09:04,860 --> 00:09:06,370
Because I don't like your acting.

117
00:09:06,370 --> 00:09:08,700
What if the other person betrays them?

118
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:11,870
But seriously, why is he
acting like this to me?

119
00:09:11,870 --> 00:09:14,420
What did I do wrong?

120
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:18,280
He's the one who suddenly lost contact,
why is he taking it out on me...

121
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:23,760
I miss you so much.

122
00:09:23,970 --> 00:09:24,720
Huh?

123
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:28,720
If so, why did you say you miss me

124
00:09:29,390 --> 00:09:31,470
and kiss me?

125
00:09:38,730 --> 00:09:39,980
You've passed.

126
00:09:38,730 --> 00:09:39,980
[You've passed.]

127
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,320
Oh!

128
00:09:41,020 --> 00:09:46,350
[But on one condition: you have to spend
a night with Jung Yihyun.]

129
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:44,530
But on one condition:

130
00:09:44,530 --> 00:09:47,200
you have to spend
a night with Jung Yihyun.

131
00:10:05,010 --> 00:10:06,950
[The Mermaid Prince]

132
00:10:11,010 --> 00:10:14,150
[To K, this script is written for you.]

133
00:10:15,230 --> 00:10:17,440
That's mine.

134
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:25,070
What's wrong?

135
00:10:25,950 --> 00:10:27,700
Wait a minute.

136
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,200
What's wrong?

137
00:10:29,530 --> 00:10:30,530
Oh, wait a minute.

138
00:11:15,290 --> 00:11:17,660
So Luka noticed something at this point,

139
00:11:17,660 --> 00:11:19,210
which is why he said that.

140
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,960
Ah, so that's why
the emotion is like this.

141
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:26,090
How about Luka jumping into the sea...

142
00:11:27,590 --> 00:11:28,470
sir?

143
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:32,010
Well, I think when emotions
reach a peak,

144
00:11:32,010 --> 00:11:34,010
one might actually do that...

145
00:11:35,350 --> 00:11:36,140
sir.

146
00:11:36,140 --> 00:11:37,930
Let's change it to that, then.

147
00:11:44,150 --> 00:11:49,240
This reminds me of the past.

148
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:52,530
Didn't we also analyze scripts
back in high school?

149
00:11:52,530 --> 00:11:54,660
Then let's change it to
Eden looking for Luka.

150
00:11:54,660 --> 00:11:58,750
Was it "Hamlet" back then?

151
00:11:58,750 --> 00:12:00,580
Ah, it was "King Lear."

152
00:12:00,580 --> 00:12:01,500
The next scene.

153
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:03,710
Ah, it was "Romeo and Juliet."

154
00:12:03,710 --> 00:12:05,290
And we were discussing
who would play Romeo.

155
00:12:05,290 --> 00:12:06,950
"A Midsummer Night's Dream."

156
00:12:08,050 --> 00:12:10,090
It was that.

157
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:14,600
Really?

158
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:17,530
Since you remembered,
why didn't you say so earlier?

159
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:20,100
Because those things aren't important.

160
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:22,690
Let's just focus on
reading this script for now.

161
00:12:22,690 --> 00:12:23,730
Director.

162
00:12:24,730 --> 00:12:26,860
Can I be nosy and ask you one more thing?

163
00:12:26,860 --> 00:12:27,820
Go ahead.

164
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:30,820
The condition was that I spend a night
with you, right?

165
00:12:33,070 --> 00:12:35,910
How are we going
to spend this night, Director?

166
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:51,340
Director?

167
00:12:54,890 --> 00:12:56,850
A night?

168
00:12:56,850 --> 00:12:58,710
Yihyun said something like that?

169
00:13:00,470 --> 00:13:02,180
You're heading home, right?

170
00:13:02,180 --> 00:13:03,770
Shall we...

171
00:13:04,350 --> 00:13:06,770
I was going to check the warehouse first.

172
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:10,530
What about dinner?

173
00:13:11,570 --> 00:13:13,570
I can skip it.

174
00:13:13,570 --> 00:13:14,910
See you tomorrow.

175
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:16,700
Wait!

176
00:13:24,210 --> 00:13:25,330
Let's go.

177
00:13:25,670 --> 00:13:26,500
What?

178
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:28,340
Today is perfect.

179
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:31,050
Sir, 2 candied haws, please.

180
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:36,090
Don't tell me

181
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:39,140
this is your first time
eating candied haws?

182
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:42,890
I am very strict about my figure.

183
00:13:43,850 --> 00:13:45,230
I used to be an actor too.

184
00:13:48,190 --> 00:13:50,400
Hey, isn't that Jung Yihyun?

185
00:13:50,820 --> 00:13:53,780
Yes, it really is him.

186
00:13:53,780 --> 00:13:55,570
We need to take pictures.

187
00:13:55,570 --> 00:13:57,100
Hurry up and take pictures!

188
00:13:58,490 --> 00:14:02,350
If you're done eating, shall we
do something to maintain your figure?

189
00:14:02,830 --> 00:14:03,620
Run!

190
00:14:27,020 --> 00:14:29,900
As a director,
I should be choosing Kang Jae-on.

191
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:48,000
Professionalism.

192
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,380
Professionalism...

193
00:15:00,510 --> 00:15:02,970
Then...

194
00:15:02,970 --> 00:15:06,930
I'll just make him reject it.

195
00:15:06,930 --> 00:15:10,350
Although I really want to work with him,

196
00:15:10,350 --> 00:15:13,190
I can't help it if he doesn't want to.

197
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:15,690
[Kang Jae-on]
[You've passed.]

198
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,690
You've passed.

199
00:15:15,690 --> 00:15:17,900
But on one condition:

200
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:20,280
you have to spend
a night with Jung Yihyun.

201
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:20,280
[But on one condition: you have to spend
a night with Jung Yihyun.]

202
00:15:30,290 --> 00:15:33,960
Okay, see you at the theater tomorrow!

203
00:15:30,290 --> 00:15:31,780
[Okay!
See you at the theater tomorrow! ^^]

204
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:36,380
Why are we meeting at the theater?
